@prefix biro:    <http://purl.org/spar/biro/> .
@prefix dcterms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .
@prefix foaf:    <http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/> .
@prefix MLDCAT:  <https://semiceu.github.io/MLDCAT-AP/releases/2.0.0/> .
@prefix lpwc:    <https://linkedpaperswithcode.com/class/> .
@prefix rdf:     <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix spdx:    <http://spdx.org/rdf/terms#> .
@prefix xsd:     <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# MODEL
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

<https://shehabeldeenayman.github.io/Gent-Terneuzen-canal/forecaster_v2>
    a MLDCAT:MachineLearningModel ;
    dcterms:title       "LSTM Seq2Seq Water Conductivity Forecaster v2" ;
    dcterms:created     "2026-05-22T00:00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    MLDCAT:version         "2.0.0" ;
    dcterms:license     <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/> ;

    MLDCAT:hasOutputFilePrediction
        <https://shehabeldeenayman.github.io/Gent-Terneuzen-canal/model.json> ;

    MLDCAT:hasRepository
        <https://shehabeldeenayman.github.io/Gent-Terneuzen-canal/tree/main> ;

    MLDCAT:hasUploader
        <https://github.com/shehabeldeenayman> ;

    MLDCAT:trainedOn
        <http://example.com/Gent-Terneuzen/conductivityDataset> ;

    MLDCAT:intendedUse """This model is designed to forecast average water conductivity along the Gent-Terneuzen canal over a 72-hour horizon at 15-minute resolution.

The model is served as a TensorFlow.js graph-model and can be loaded directly in a browser:
  const model = await tf.loadGraphModel('https://shehabeldeenayman.github.io/Gent-Terneuzen-canal/model.json');
  const output = model.predict(inputTensor);   // inputTensor shape [1, 1344, 1]""" ;

    MLDCAT:limitations """1. The model was trained exclusively on conductivity data from the Gent-Terneuzen canal. Applying it to other waterways or sensor configurations will likely degrade performance without retraining.
2. The input window must be exactly 1344 time steps. Shorter or irregular sequences are not supported without additional preprocessing.
3. Forecasting accuracy degrades over the horizon: error (MAE/RMSE) increases progressively beyond the 24-hour mark (step 96).
4. The MinMax scaler (scaler_v2.pkl) fitted on the training split must be applied to the input before inference and used to inverse-transform the output. Using a different scaler will produce incorrect results.
5. The model does not account for external covariates (e.g. tidal cycles, weather, vessel traffic) that may affect conductivity.""" .


# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# OUTPUT FILE  — TensorFlow.js graph-model
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

<https://shehabeldeenayman.github.io/Gent-Terneuzen-canal/model.json>
    a MLDCAT:OutputFilePrediction ;
    dcterms:title      "forecasterTensorFlow.js graph-model" ;
    dcterms:identifier "forecaster.json" ;
    dcterms:format     <http://example.com/format/tfjs-graph-model> ;
    MLDCAT:url            <https://shehabeldeenayman.github.io/Gent-Terneuzen-canal/model.json> ;
    spdx:checksum      <http://example.com/Checksum/forecaster_v2_json> .

# <http://example.com/Checksum/forecaster_v2_json>
#     a spdx:Checksum ;
#     spdx:algorithm     spdx:checksumAlgorithm_sha256 ;
#     spdx:checksumValue ""^^xsd:hexBinary .


